      "id": "chem11-p231-a5",
      "en": "K_sp is called the solubility product. In general, the solubility product[scan obscured] substance is the product of molar concentrations of its ions in the satur[scan obscured] solution each raised to an exponent equal to the coefficient of each ion in[scan obscured] balanced equation. K_sp is usually very small quantity at room temperature.[scan obscured] value of K_sp is temperature dependent. In general, for a sparingly sol[scan obscured] substance, AₓB_y the equilibrium equation is",
